---
description: Win32 and unsafe rules for LightCapture recording code
globs: "**/*.rs"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Windows unsafe

- Prefer the `windows` crate’s safe wrappers. Keep `unsafe` in small functions next to the FFI.
- Every `unsafe` block needs a `// SAFETY:` comment listing the invariants.
- Enable `#![deny(unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn)]` in crates that contain `unsafe`.
- Never `Map` a capture `ID3D11Texture2D` to CPU on the encode path. Frames stay on the GPU until the encoder takes them.
- COM/WinRT objects must have clear ownership (drop order, `Release` via the wrapper). Do not clone raw pointers without documenting aliasing.
- Isolate WGC, Media Foundation, and WASAPI behind modules in `lightcapture-core`, not in the app crate.
